# DO wine.skip-synth-playout
#
# For a game whose sounds go through DirectMusic and that sits on its loading
# screen for minutes, logging err:dmsynth:synth_sink_render_thread
# "WaitForMultipleObjects returned 0" every second and a half or so: Game
# Maker 7's games, which give every sound a DirectMusic performance of its
# own and stop it again as they load. Wine 10's synthesiser plays out its
# two-second buffer each time one stops; this makes it stop at once, in this
# stage's own Wine (its 32-bit dmsynth.dll), as Wine 11.2 and later do. Use it
# in place of winetricks' directmusic, whose Microsoft dsound.dll leaves
# DirectShow's music (MCI's MP3s) silent. Put it after the stage has Wine
# (FROM --module=wine… prefix); a game without it gets Wine as it comes.
# docs/modules.md#the-wine-modules-patches has the details.
FUNCTION skip-synth-playout
  WINE.SKIP-SYNTH-PLAYOUT
END
